<section class="container mt-5 pt-5">
    <div class="row mt-3">
        <div class="col-lg-12 section-title">
            <div class="testimonial-heading">
                <h2 class="title">Key Factors to Consider When Choosing a University</h2>
                <span class="shape-line"><i class="icon-19"></i></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>1. Program Availability</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">Look for universities that are renowned for your chosen field of study. Confirm that the university offers the specific course or specialization you’re interested in. Go through the curriculum to ensure it matches your academic and professional aspirations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>2. Budget and Affordability</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">Compare tuition fees and living costs across universities. You should look for scholarships, grants, or financial aid options offered by the university. Must consider whether the university provides affordable on-campus housing or other cost-saving options.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>3. Location and Lifestyle</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                Think about the university’s location, climate, and proximity to major cities. Check if the cultural environment suits your lifestyle and preferences or not. Most importantly, check if the location offers opportunities for internships, part-time jobs, or industry exposure.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>4. Post-Study Opportunities</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                Research the university’s career services and job placement stats. Look into post-study work visa policies in the country and check if the university has strong ties with industries and employers in your field.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>5. University Reputation and Alumni Network</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                A university with a strong reputation can enhance your resume and open doors to global opportunities. Explore the alumni network to see how graduates have progressed in their careers.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>6. Student Support Services</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                Look for universities that offer robust support for international students, including orientation programs, counseling, and academic assistance. Check if they provide language support, career guidance, and help with visa or accommodation.
            </p>
        </div>


        <div class="mt-3">
            <h4>7. Campus Facilities and Student Life</h4>
            <p class="mt-3">
                A vibrant campus life can make your study abroad experience more enjoyable. Explore the university’s facilities, such as libraries, labs, sports centres, and student clubs. Also, make sure if the university promotes diversity and inclusivity.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>




