            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <<div class="accordion" id="accordionPanelsStayOpenExample">
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button fs-3" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#panelsStayOpen-collapseOne" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="panelsStayOpen-collapseOne">
                    1. How do I choose the right university for my field of study?
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="panelsStayOpen-collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
                <div class="accordion-body fs-4">
                    Start by identifying your academic and career goals. Research universities that are renowned for your chosen field and check their global rankings, faculty expertise, and available programs. Look into the curriculum to ensure it aligns with your aspirations and offers opportunities for internships or research.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#panelsStayOpen-collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panelsStayOpen-collapseTwo">
                    2. What factors should I consider when selecting a university abroad?
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="panelsStayOpen-collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                <div class="accordion-body fs-4">
                    Key factors include the university’s reputation, program availability, tuition fees, living costs, location, post-study opportunities, and student support services. Additionally, consider the cultural environment, language of instruction, and visa policies of the country where the university is located.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#panelsStayOpen-collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panelsStayOpen-collapseThree">
                    3. How important are university rankings when making a decision?
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="panelsStayOpen-collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                <div class="accordion-body fs-4">
                    University rankings can provide a general idea of academic quality and reputation, but they shouldn’t be the sole deciding factor. Focus on rankings specific to your field of study, as well as other aspects like faculty expertise, research opportunities, and alumni success.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

         <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#panelsStayOpen-collapsefour" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panelsStayOpen-collapseThree">
                    4. Are scholarships available for international students?
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="panelsStayOpen-collapsefour" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                <div class="accordion-body fs-4">
                    Yes, many universities and countries offer scholarships for international students. These can be merit-based, need-based, or specific to certain programs. Research the scholarships offered by your target universities and explore government or private funding options like Erasmus+ or country-specific programs.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button fs-3 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#panelsStayOpen-collapsefive" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panelsStayOpen-collapseThree">
                    5. How can I ensure the university is a good fit for me?
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="panelsStayOpen-collapsefive" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                <div class="accordion-body fs-4">
                    Visit the university’s website to learn about its programs, campus facilities, and student life. Reach out to current students or alumni for insights, and join online forums or social media groups. Consider factors like location, class sizes, cultural fit, and the availability of support services for international students. Trust your instincts and choose a university that feels right for you academically, financially, and personally.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>